comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T20:54:19.962Z",codex-sol,"Baseline reproduction before code changes: built the package with npm run build, initialized a scratch pm project through the installed real CLI, created a synthetic issue, and dispatched the built web status extension through the real SDK testing engine. The staged workflow had an attested sibling plus an unattested path. pm-ops 2026.10.4 rejects PUB=\"npm publish\"; $PUB --access public, but returns zero failures for an enabled alias ship=\"npm publish\" followed by ship --access public and for ship() { npm \"$@\"; } followed by ship publish --access public. These are live publish paths masked by the attested sibling. Preserve canonical resolution, add fail-closed checks at the consumer boundary, and cover both verdicts where supported; unsupported indirection must fail even with a provenance-looking argument."
  "2026-10-07T21:05:35.956Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only auditPublishAttestation with return canonicalAudit(sources), leaving imports, verify, launcher and test files unchanged. The targeted suite loaded and ran 45 tests: 27 passed and 18 failed with assertion failures, including alias and forwarded-function publishing; no module-loading or syntax failures. Restored the exact implementation bytes and reran the complete focused suite. Supplemental checks also reject partial executable substitutions, unknown publish flags, executable arrays and cross-step provenance evidence; supported attested scalar commands, literal functions/evaluators and quoted provenance flags remain accepted. pm test --run --progress passed; automatic test-result persistence is disabled by repository policy, so evidence is recorded in comments."
  "2026-10-07T21:05:36.844Z",codex-sol,"Canonical convergence is tracked separately as pm-web-vyxu. No changes were made to pm-ops or hosted services. README and docs/publish-attestation.md describe supported syntax, conservative rejections and the canonical change needed."
  "2026-10-07T21:10:42.405Z",codex-sol,"Default worktree npm release:check ran 534 tests: 523 passed, 11 failed, zero skipped. Three failures are the existing catalog worktree-discovery/snapshot blockers (pm-web-cqwm and pm-web-s99c); eight arise from extensionless CommonJS fixtures inheriting shared scratch ESM metadata. With an isolated CommonJS scratch root the affected 26-test launcher/route subset passes. Will also verify unchanged gates at the committed head in a standalone copy inside the package worktree, matching CI layout; this measures committed snapshot invariants rather than live fleet freshness."
  "2026-10-07T21:12:51.902Z",codex-sol,"Additional SDK integration observation: initializing a scratch pm tracker underneath an existing Git checkout configures enclosing Git merge attributes for that nested tracker. Tests must initialize their own Git repository first or keep scratch trackers outside checkout ancestry. The new regression helper now initializes Git before pm. Generated scratch merge-attribute additions from validation will be restored to the original tracked file; no SDK API bug was established or filed."
  "2026-10-07T21:14:16.759Z",codex-sol,"Worktree Bun release:check also executed at unchanged thresholds. With in-checkout scratch storage it ran 492 tests, 483 passed and 9 failed, zero skipped: catalog worktree discovery plus scratch-source visibility, ancestor dependency lookup and explicit-tracker selection. Its measured source metrics were 90.28% statements/lines, 79.50% branches and 93.90% functions, but failed tests invalidate the gate. Scratch storage is now outside Git ancestry with explicit CommonJS metadata; the new helper also sets an explicit fixture pm path before init/create/get. Restored all validation-generated enclosing merge attributes. Standalone validation will retain the same source/test sets and thresholds."
  "2026-10-07T21:15:23.965Z",codex-sol,"Final linked build/typecheck/focused test command passes after explicit fixture isolation: 54 tests passed, zero failed and zero skipped. npm and Bun release checks will now run on a committed standalone copy using the unchanged configured thresholds (90% statements, 90% lines, 79% branches, 92% functions) and zero duplication. Worktree/live-fleet failures remain separately linked instead of being suppressed or fixed outside scope."
  "2026-10-07T21:15:57.319Z",codex-sol,"Correction to the preceding final-linked-suite claim: that rerun failed because the copied TypeScript launcher inherited the new CommonJS scratch-root metadata and could not load as ESM. The earlier 54-test pass remains valid for its earlier environment, but it is not evidence for this rerun. Fixed the regression helper to declare its own module type before copying the ESM launcher. Will rerun and record the measured verdict; no gate pass is claimed for the failed run."
  "2026-10-07T21:17:51.477Z",codex-sol,"Measured rerun after declaring fixture module type: pm test --run --progress exits zero; all 54 focused tests pass with no skips. Repeated the behavioral audit-only revert in the isolated scratch environment: 45 tests execute, 27 pass and 18 fail on assertions, including alias and argument-forwarding paths, with no syntax or module-loading failures. Restored the exact implementation afterward."
  "2026-10-07T21:27:18.031Z",codex-sol,"Final review expanded the adversarial corpus to combined indirection. The real inert Bash publisher confirms variable-routed aliases/evaluators and variable-routed function argument forwarding execute publish without provenance. All 66 focused tests now pass through pm test --run --progress. Reverting only auditPublishAttestation executes 57 tests: 29 pass and 28 fail on assertions, with zero syntax/module-load failures and zero skips. Exact implementation restored. Earlier standalone npm/Bun release checks passed at the earlier commit; rerunning both on the expanded final implementation before reporting completion."
  "2026-10-07T21:40:47.822Z",codex-sol,"The final 71-test corpus also covers unresolved publisher paths and compound executable-word forwarding ($NPM$@), while retaining a literal scalar path control. pm test --run --progress passes all 71 tests, zero failed or skipped. The audit-only behavioral revert executes 62 tests: 30 pass and 32 fail on assertions; real Bash forwarding still reaches publish without provenance. No load/syntax failures. Exact implementation restored. Commit 0c05b57 passed both standalone npm and Bun release checks: 546 tests each, zero skipped, 33 configured source files at 90.23% statements/lines, 79.41% branches and 93.90% functions; production audit zero, packed npm/Bun acceptance and remaining gates passed. Rerunning the complete gates on the final corpus and guard before push."
  "2026-10-07T21:51:28.563Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit a7233d1 passes both npm run release:check and bun run release:check in the standalone CI layout. Each runs 551 tests with zero failed or skipped. Configured coverage covers 33 source files: npm 90.23% statements/lines, 79.41% branches, 93.90% functions; Bun 90.23% statements/lines, 79.42% branches, 93.90% functions, against unchanged 90/90/79/92 thresholds. Duplication zero; typechecks, lint, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), pack dry run, packed npm and native Bun consumer acceptance, changelog check, release-date gate and attestation gate all pass. Default worktree/live-fleet catalog blockers remain pm-web-cqwm and pm-web-s99c; fixture isolation follow-up is pm-web-jp0u and canonical auditor convergence is pm-web-vyxu. No SDK API defect was established or filed. Final metadata commit and exact-head gate repeat will be reported in the PR."
  "2026-10-07T21:56:25.515Z",codex-sol,"Final review reproduced an additional false pass before correction: a literal NPM=npm binding followed by xargs $NPM --provenance accepts publish --no-provenance from stdin. Spawned publishers have unknown runtime argument sources even when a literal provenance flag is present. Add fail-closed xargs and parallel regressions plus an attested npx control before final verification."
  "2026-10-07T21:59:18.045Z",codex-sol,"Expanded focused suite passes all 75 tests with zero skips. The added cases reject literal and scalar-routed xargs input and parallel publishers even with a provenance flag, while a literal attested npx npm invocation still passes. The canonical scanner strips spawning prefixes in resolved invocation reports; original shell commands retain the canonical spawnedAsCommand evidence used by this guard."
  "2026-10-07T22:00:20.059Z",codex-sol,"Final behavioral revert proof replaces only auditPublishAttestation with return canonicalAudit(sources), retaining all imports, the real launcher, fixture and tests. The targeted corpus executes 66 tests: 35 assertion failures, 31 passes, zero skips and no module-load failures. The script is restored byte-for-byte. Restored focused suite and both unchanged-threshold release gates will be run on the updated public package; standalone catalog scope remains distinct from live-fleet blockers."
  "2026-10-07T22:01:56.496Z",codex-sol,"Restored PM-linked command passed: npm run build && npm run build:test && node --test test/publish-indirection.test.ts test/verify-release-publish-attestation.test.ts. All 75 tests pass, zero failures or skips; pm test --run --progress exits zero. Direct tracked-source gate also passes. Commit this correction before full npm and Bun release checks in the standalone CI layout, retaining all configured coverage thresholds and source lists."
  "2026-10-07T22:18:02.413Z",codex-sol,"Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass at implementation commit 2f2652d in independent standalone CI layouts. Each executes 555 tests with zero failures or skips. Coverage: 33 configured source files, statements/lines 90.23%, branches 79.41%, functions 93.90%, unchanged thresholds 90/90/79/92. Duplication is zero (0/45043 lines, 151 sources), production audit zero vulnerabilities, and packed npm-current/native bun-current acceptance passes with host SDK 2026.10.4 and identical tarball hashes. Typecheck, lint, docstrings, pack dry run, changelog/date and publish-attestation checks pass. Live-fleet catalog and scratch-fixture follow-ups remain open; standalone results establish committed-snapshot invariants. Final receipt commit will change only tracker/docs, with executable-input equivalence and affected metadata checks verified before push. No SDK API bug was established; explicit tracker paths, nested merge-attribute initialization and disabled linked-test result persistence are documented integration boundaries."
  "2026-10-11T04:58:49.764Z",codex-attestation,Resuming PR #176 only. Merge current main while retaining the conservative publish guard and SDK 2026.10.10 changes; rerun guard-only revert proof and full npm/Bun release gates with unchanged source/test lists and thresholds in a standalone CI layout with isolated scratch metadata and Git identity. Leave the item in_progress and release the claim after verification.
  "2026-10-11T05:02:25.167Z",codex-attestation,"Main merge preserved the publish audit unchanged and exact SDK 2026.10.10, pm-ops 2026.10.6 and graph/catalog changes. PM drivers unioned both branches on pm-web-cqwm and pm-web-s99c. Reconciliation dry-run has trusted driver receipts; the sole reported discarded tests event reflects source_kind changing from local_mutation to merge_union, with all five test commands, paths and authors retained. Accept this metadata-only reconciliation; no test or comment is removed."
  "2026-10-11T05:08:51.143Z",codex-attestation,"Merged focused audit suite: 75 passed, zero failed/skipped. Runtime was 327 seconds under concurrent verification load. Replace only the linked command timeout from 180 to 900 seconds; preserve its exact build/test command and all assertions. Full release gates retain identical source/test lists and thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T05:12:15.875Z",codex-attestation,"Guard-only revert proof rerun against merged SDK/auditor pins: replacing only auditPublishAttestation with canonicalAudit preserves imports, launcher and tests; the adversarial corpus executes and fails behavioral assertions. Restored the original audit bytes and verified identical SHA-256 b6e5283f64625ef495c7e811378c0af8cfa052fe8e15834be694d8cfbb0d38ed. npm release gates have passed typecheck, lint, zero duplication and documented declarations; full counts will follow. Reconciliation validates all 147 item histories with zero drift."
  "2026-10-11T05:15:29.281Z",codex-attestation,"pm test pm-web-szow --run --progress passed its unchanged linked build/test command: 75 tests passed, zero failures/skips, trusted local source context and no mismatch. Guard-only revert: 67 executed, 35 assertion failures and 32 passes, zero skipped; original SHA-256 restored. Complete npm release suite remains running; no full gate pass is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-11T05:24:36.348Z",codex-attestation,"Full npm release validation recorded an unrelated main graph timing failure: the existing 2000-item read took 33115 ms against its unchanged 10000 ms bound. Keep the failure receipt and complete the full suite; do not relax limits, hide tests or alter graph code in the attestation task. Diagnose whether this reproduces independently before claiming any release pass."
  "2026-10-11T05:41:27.355Z",codex-attestation,"npm release:check completed its full configured suite: 559 tests, 557 passed, 2 failed, zero skipped. Failures: the existing 2000-item graph bound (33115 ms versus 10000 ms) and spawn-overlap startup ordering; same-workspace serialization passed. Printed aggregate coverage is 90.28 percent statements/lines, 80.04 branches, 93.06 functions, against unchanged 90/90/79/92 thresholds. Test failures prevent a gate pass and invalidate the coverage receipt; preserve the raw log. Bun full validation and the npm tail gates are running separately."
  "2026-10-11T05:45:53.668Z",codex-attestation,"The orchestrator intentionally interrupted the attempted local Bun release gate, npm remaining-tail run and old CLI session under extreme shared-host contention. Neither interrupted run has a passing verdict. Retain completed local npm 559/557/2/0, focused and PM-linked 75/75, and guard-only revert 67 executed with 35 failures caused by behavioral assertions and byte-exact restoration. Copy only the authorized existing CI workflow: Node 22/26 jobs execute literal npm run release:check and bun run release:check with fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration. Sources, test lists, assertions and thresholds remain unchanged. Independent PR #176 CI is pending; no results from another PR establish this head."
  "2026-10-11T05:47:19.517Z",codex-attestation,"Final lightweight verification: authorized CI file is byte-identical to the supplied workflow; YAML parses, Node 22/26 jobs contain both exact literal gates with isolated Git identity, and the supplemental plus complete tracked-source attestation audits pass. Runtime source, tests, package pins and built output match merge commit 58ebab7, so retain the completed 75/75 acceptance and guard-only proof without another heavy rerun. Reconciliation dry-run passes with zero drift, zero repairs and zero pending receipts. Strict local PM health fails on extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (2026.10.10 versus 2026.10.11 for pm-github); 13 stale in-progress items are advisory. Preserve that local environment boundary; independent CI uses the committed installer pin. Leave szow in_progress and all follow-ups open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-11T06:03:25.040Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator independent verification passes the final focused audit suites 75/75 with zero skips. Independent CI run 38116108000 on implementation head 06f50e6 passes literal npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26: each 559/559 tests, zero failures/skips, all 34 configured server sources meeting unchanged thresholds, all four packed npm/Bun current/minimum-host scenarios accepted, strict fresh-checkout PM health and committed dist checks passing. Preserve the complete local 557/559 timing failure, interrupted Bun/tail receipts and local managed-extension skew as separate boundaries. Recording these final receipts changes only documentation and tracker evidence; runtime/test inputs stay identical."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T22:12:25.943Z",codex,"author=claude\ncreated_at=now\ntext=shellScalars indexed only quoted assignments, so a bare NPM=npm was never recorded. expandScalars then left $NPM unresolved, tokenizeCommands saw a program named \"$NPM\" rather than npm, and the line was not recognised as a publish at all. Because the workflow's own legitimate attested publish still satisfied the non-vacuity guard, auditPublishAttestation returned zero failures and the gate reported a clean pass over a workflow containing an unattested publish. The gate was blind rather than wrong, which is the failure mode that keeps a gate trusted while it is not looking.\n\nMeasured behaviourally across the fleet rather than by reading the sources, by importing each repository's own verify-release-publish-attestation.ts and auditing a fixture holding one attested publish plus one variable-routed unattested publish. 12 of 17 repositories returned failures=0: pm-graph, pm-starter, pm-csv, pm-context, pm-web, pm-presets, pm-ts-starter, pm-todos, pm-linear, pm-brief, pm-github and pm-slack-standup. 5 already caught it: pm-jira, pm-beads, pm-ops, pm-slack and pm-gantt-chart.\n\nFix: shellScalars accepts a third alternative for an unquoted single-word value, matching what pm-jira already carries. The existing guard that refuses to inline a value containing a substitution, backtick, quote or parenthesis is unchanged, so a value that would change how its line parses is still never inlined.\n\nThe regression test asserts the audit-level property rather than the map contents, so it fails for the reason the gate exists: with the fix reverted it reports failures=0 where 1 is required. The neighbouring assertion that an unquoted value cannot hold a command encoded the old behaviour as intentional and was updated to match, exactly as pm-jira updated it.\n\nThis is the fifth time this class of bypass has been fixed in one vendored copy while the others stayed exposed. The root cause is that the verifier is vendored into every package instead of being consumed from pm-ops; that is tracked in the companion repository as pm-cli-website-bunt."
  "2026-08-28T22:36:35.385Z",claude,"Bot review on the first round (Greptile P1 x2, Sourcery x2) found that reading scalar assignments out of the raw text indexes bindings the shell never makes. All four were reproduced before fixing:\n1. A name defined only in a COMMENT was indexed. `# FLAG=--provenance` followed by `npm publish --access public $FLAG` audited as attested and returned zero failures: an unattested publish borrowed its flag from a comment and passed the gate. This is a bypass, and it pre-dates the unquoted-value change because the quoted form (`# CMD=\"npm publish\"`) was indexed the same way.\n2. A name inside a quoted argument was indexed. `echo \"config NPM=npm\"` bound NPM, so a later literal `$NPM publish` was audited as an npm publish the shell never runs.\n3. An unquoted value continuing into an expansion was truncated to its prefix. `NPM=npm$SUFFIX` bound NPM to `npm`; the literal guard then saw no `$` because the `$` had been excluded from the capture, so a value the scan cannot resolve was treated as one it could.\n4. The docstring still said only quoted values are indexed.\nFixed by reading assignments from tokenizeCommands instead of from raw text. The tokeniser has already dropped comments and resolved quoting, so a word is only treated as an assignment where the shell would treat it as one; it keeps `$SUFFIX` inside the word, so the literal guard sees the whole value rather than a prefix; and only a command-leading word can assign, so `npm publish FOO=bar` is an argument rather than a binding.\nOne consequence found by the existing suite rather than by a bot: the tokeniser consumes a substitution instead of keeping its text, so `SUBST=\"$(node -p 1)\"` arrives as an empty value that the literal guard would accept. Inlining it would ERASE `$SUBST` from the command, turning \"not understood\" into \"carries no flags\" — the exact false-pass this module already warns about. Empty values are therefore never indexed.\nBoth new tests were observed failing against the previous implementation and passing after. Verified behaviourally in all 17 packages carrying this file: the comment bypass, the quoted-argument binding, the truncation and the substitution are all refused, while `NPM=npm`, `CMD=\"npm publish\"` and a leading `FOO=bar` still resolve."
  "2026-08-28T22:57:41.395Z",claude,"Round 3. Greptile raised three further P1 security findings against the tokeniser-based implementation, and all three reproduced:\n1. Substitution suffix. `NPM=npm$(printf foo)` — the tokeniser consumes the substitution before the literal guard sees the value, so NPM was bound to the prefix `npm`. The scan then analysed a different command from the one the shell runs.\n2. Command-scoped assignment leaked file-wide. `FLAG=--provenance some-command` binds only for that one command, but it was stored in the file-global map, so a LATER `npm publish --access public $FLAG` was rewritten into an attested-looking publish. Audit returned zero failures: a false pass.\n3. Subshell escape. `$(FLAG=--provenance)` is a binding the outer shell never sees, but the recursive tokeniser returns the nested command and its assignment was promoted into the outer map. Also a false pass, also measured at zero failures.\nReplaced the rule rather than patching three more cases. A name is now taken only from a line that is EXACTLY one assignment carrying a fully literal value, anchored at both ends. Anchoring closes the truncation pair, because a value that does not reach the end of the line is not the value. Requiring the line to hold nothing else closes the comment, quoted-argument, command-scoped and subshell cases in one rule instead of four special cases. Escapes are honoured so `NPM=npm\\ publish` still holds a command in one word, which was a Sourcery finding, and the existing refusal of any value carrying a substitution, backtick, quote or parenthesis now applies after unescaping.\n`FOO=bar npm publish` is deliberately no longer indexed. It is command-scoped, and the publish on that same line is visible to the scan directly, so nothing is lost.\nVerified across all 17 packages carrying this file by exercising 16 properties against each package's own verifier rather than by comparing files. The two regression tests were observed failing against the previous implementation and passing after.\nOne finding was accepted as valid but deliberately left out of this change: scalars are still resolved from a file-wide map, so a later assignment can rewrite an earlier use. Raised by Sourcery, reproduced, and filed as companion item pm-cli-website-1j4o because it is a different defect needing position-aware resolution."
